{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]) & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T([\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]) & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T([\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]) & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T([\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]) & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535300 true] [17592186106418 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535300 true] [17592186106418 1100 "A linear transformation $T$ represents a stretch along the $x$-axis or $y$-axis. Given that $v = \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}$ and $T(v) = \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}$, what is the standard matrix of $T$?" 13194139535300 false] [17592186106418 1100 "A linear transformation $T$ represents a stretch along the $x$-axis or $y$-axis. Given that $v=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]$ and $T(v)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],$ what is the standard matrix of $T?$" 13194139535300 true] [17592186106418 1145 "First, we are told that $T$ represents a stretch along the $x$-axis or $y$-axis.\n\nComparing the $x$- and $y$-components of $v$ and $T(v),$ we note the following:\n\n- the $x$-components of $v$ and $T(v)$ are the same, while\n\n- the $y$-component of $T(v)$ is $\\frac{1}{3}$ times the $y$-component of $v.$\n\nSo, we conclude that $T$ represents a stretch of scale factor $\\frac{1}{3}$ in the $y$-direction.\n\nTherefore, the standard matrix of $T$ is\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139535300 true] [17592186106419 109