veloper/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062085/assets/dae63d7007d115438139be51862d878deadd1ed300b3b870935c2cbe44edaef3.png" 13194139535300 true] [17592186342585 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535300 true] [17592186342585 1111 #uuid "a54a940b-885e-5cb5-9997-21b1f954a859" 13194139535300 true] [17592186342586 1017 #edb/ref 17592186342587 13194139535300 true] [17592186342586 1017 #edb/ref 17592186342589 13194139535300 true] [17592186342586 1017 #edb/ref 17592186342591 13194139535300 true] [17592186342586 1089 "q-317606" 13194139535300 true] [17592186342586 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535300 true] [17592186342586 1100 "A linear transformation $T$ represents a stretch along the $x$-axis or $y$-axis. Given that $u=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]$ and $T(u)=[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],$ what is the standard matrix of $T?$\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $T=\\,\\,$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  |  | $0$ | {{field-3}} |  |" 13194139535300 true] [17592186342586 1113 #uuid "4879405b-2d19-5d7e-99f6-9f2899744e7a" 13194139535300 true] [17592186342586 1145 "First, we are told that $T$ represents a stretch along the $x$-axis or $y$-axis.\n\nComparing the $x$- and $y$-components of $u$ and $T(u),$ we note the following:\n\n- the $y$-components of $u$ and $T(u)$ are the same, while\n\n- the $x$-component of $T(u)$ is $3$ times the $x$-component of $u.$\n\nSo, we conclude that $T$ represents a stretch of scale factor $3$ in the $x$-direction. \n\nTherefore, the standard matrix of $T$ is\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139535300 true] [17592186342587 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342588 13194139535300 true] [17592186342587 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535300 true] [17592186342587 1041 "field-1" 13194139535300 true] [17592186342587 1104 #edb/ref 17592186342588 13194139535300 true] [17592186342587 1110 #uuid "933df4d0-3509-5e79-bee9-96659673b0f8" 13194139535300 true] [17592186342588 1034 "3" 13194139535300 true] [17592186342588 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535300 true] [17592186342588 1111 #uuid "7baaa823-4317-5893-8760-58522db305c3" 13194139535300 true] [17592186342589 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342590 13194139535300 true] [17592186342589 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535300 true] [17592186342589 1041 "field-2" 13194139535300 true] [17592186342589 1104 #edb/ref 17592186342590 13194139535300 true] [17592186342589 1110 #uuid "ac01ecf7-6a98-5a9f-9280-2eb5a9d411d0" 13194139535300 true] [17592186342590 1034 "0" 13194139535300 true] [17592186342590 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535300 true] [17592186342590 1111 #uuid "51f3b604-b001-538c-8b3c-6f6cd8a80111" 13194139535300 true] [17592186342591 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342592 13194139535300 true] [17592186342591 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535300 true] [17592186342591 1041 "field-3" 13194139535300 true] [17592186342591 1104 #edb/ref 17592186342592 13194139535300 true] [17592186342591 1110 #uuid "d633505d-dab1-550f-9042-2483c3b82ab9" 13194139535300 true] [17592186342592 1034 "1" 13194139535300 true] [17592186342592 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535300 true] [17592186342592 1111 #uuid "64df85fa-2ea4-575f-99f4-b40e6ba89cd2" 13194139535300 true] [17592186342593 1017 #edb/ref 17592186342594 13194139535300 true] [17592186342593 1017 #edb/ref 17592186342596 13194139535300 true] [17592186342593 1017 #edb/ref 17592186342598 13194139535300 true] [17592186342593 1089 "q-317609" 13194139535300 true] [17592186342593 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535300 true] [17592186342593 1100 "A linear transformation $T$ represents a stretch along the $x$-axis or $y$-axis. Given that $u=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]$ and $T(u)=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],$ what is the standard matrix of $T?$\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $T=\\,\\,$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  |  | $0$ | {{field-3}} |  |" 13194139535300 true] [17592186342593 1113 #uuid "269e92e7-dd9e-5a56-9cb9-162b4eeb2056" 13194139535300 true] [17592186342593 1145 "First, we are told that $T$ represents a stretch along the $x$-axis or $y$-axis.\n\nComparing the $x$- and $y$-components of $u$ and $T(u),$ we note the following:\n\n- the $y$-components of $u$ and $T(u)$ are the same, while\n\n- the $x$-component of $T(u)$ is $\\frac{1}{2}$ times the $x$-component of $u.$\n\nSo, we conclude that $T$ represents a stretch of scale factor $\\frac{1}{2}$ in the $x$-direction. \n\nTherefore, the standard matrix of $T$ is\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139535300 true] [17592186342594 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342595 13194139535300 true] [17592186342594 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535300 true] [17592186342594 1041 "field-1" 13194139535300 true] [17592186342594 1104 #edb/ref 17592186342595 13194139535300 true] [17592186342594 1110 #uuid "d8e1473c-1de5-54a0-9237-35db5a9f49d6" 13194139535300 true] [17592186342595 1034 "\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139535300 true] [17592186342595 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535300 true] [17592186342595 1111 #uuid "8bc3c941-eb66-5555-8d60-181fe24c7468" 13194139535300 true] [17592186342596 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342597 13194139535300 true] [17592186342596 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535300 true] [17592186342596 1041 "field-2" 13194139535300 true] [17592186342596 1104 #edb/ref 17592186342597 13194139535300 true] [17592186342596 1110 #uuid "856855d4-bc04-506c-9ee3-afedc09171f8" 13194139535300 true] [17592186342597 1034 "0" 13194139535300 true] [17592186342597 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535300 true] [17592186342597 1111 #uuid "d68253fd-ff6e-5953-ba8e-bf0bdc15728a" 13194139535300 true] [17592186342598 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342599 13194139535300 true] [17592186342598 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535300 true] [17592186342598 1041 "field-3" 13194139535300 true] [17592186342598 1104 #edb/ref 17592186342599 13194139535300 true] [17592186342598 1110 #uuid "517a3563-445f-5c1d-8247-ba695b632bea" 13194139535300 true] [17592186342599 1034 "1" 13194139535300 true] [17592186342599 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535300 true] [17592186342599 1111 #uuid "391aa0a5-532c-55d0-ad07-9472cf2e0701" 13194139535300 true] [17592186342600 1017 #edb/ref 17592186342601 13194139535300 true] [17592186342600 1017 #edb/ref 17592186342604 13194139535300 true] [17592186342600 1017 #edb/ref 17592186342606 13194139535300 true] [17592186342600 1017 #edb/ref 17592186342608 13194139535300 true] [17592186342600 1089 "q-317612" 13194139535300 true] [17592186342600 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535300 true] [17592186342600 1100 "A linear transformation $T$ represents a stretch along the $x$-axis or $y$-axis. Given that $u=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ and $T(u)=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ \\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}],$ what is the standard matrix of $T?$\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $T=\\,\\,$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  |  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |" 13194139535300 true] [17592186342600 1113 #uuid "964ace1f-4db9-5484-a2c3-7ffb0c8d5586" 13194139535300 true] [17592186342600 1145 "First, we are told that $T$ represents a stretch along the $x$-axis or $y$-axis.\n\nComparing the $x$- and $y$-components of $u$ and $T(u),$ we note the following:\n\n- the $x$-components of $u$ and $T(u)$ are the same, while\n\n- the $y$-component of $T(u)$ is $\\sqrt{3}$ times the $y$-component of $u.$\n\nSo, we conclude that $T$ represents a stretch of scale factor $\\sqrt{3}$ in the $y$-direction. \n\nTherefore, the standard matrix of $T$ is\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139535300 true] [17592186342601 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342602 13194139535300 true] [17592186342601 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342603 13194139535300 true] [17592186342601 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535300 true] [17592186342601 1041 "field-1" 13194139535300 true] [1759